\title{sdmTMBexperiments: Experimental Helper Functions for 'sdmTMB'}
\description{
A collection of experimental helper functions for working with spatiotemporal models from the 'sdmTMB' package: model comparison, mesh sensitivity analysis, retrospective analysis, survey-specific index comparison, prediction-grid construction, and diagnostic plotting. The package doubles as a showcase of how to use these functions and a staging ground for methods that may later be adopted into 'sdmTMB'.
}
\section{Use of generative AI}{

Much of the code, tests and documentation in this package were written with
an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5, Anthropic) from the maintainer's
prototypes and instructions. The maintainer reviewed, tested and accepted all
AI-generated material and is responsible for it. Commits made with AI
assistance carry a \code{Co-Authored-By} line in the Git history, and each
function's help page has an "AI assistance" section recording the model that
wrote it and the last model that reviewed it in full. This follows the
rOpenSci policy on generative AI in software review
(\url{https://ropensci.org/blog/2026/02/26/ropensci-ai-policy/}).
}

